## Add test-first contracts for entity SHACL facets
================================================================================

Context:
New feature: for one Graph Explorer entity (right-click, detail panel, canvas
ring) or via a new MCP tool, evaluate every SHACL shape related to its type
(own class, ancestors, global) against that entity only. Spec lives in
`.planning/entity-shacl-facets/SPEC.md`. Tests are written first (TDD) and
are intentionally red until the implementation lands; no production code is
changed in this section.

Changes:

1. tests/units/dtwin/test_node_shacl_service.py
   New. NodeShaclService contract: shape selection, inherited-shape class
   substitution, entity-filtered UNION ALL batch (escaping, hostile shape
   IDs), five statuses, observed values across the #// URI separator with a
   20-value cap, ordering, summary, per-shape fallback, rdf:type fallback.
2. tests/units/api/test_node_shacl_endpoint.py
   New. Public and internal `/nodes/shacl` routes (GET-only, entity_uri
   required) and `shacl_shape_count` on `/nodes/context` and
   `/api/v1/domain/classes`.
3. tests/units/mcp/test_shacl_facets_formatting.py
   New. `_format_shacl_facets_response` text contract and the `[Context]`
   hint in node and class blocks; unchecked shapes never read as PASS.
4. tests/units/mcp/test_domain_policy_gating.py
   Tool count 14 → 15; `check_entity_shacl_facets` backend call, hidden on
   select and refused at call time when disabled, hint gating, GRAPH_TOOLS.
5. tests/units/core/test_mcp_tools_policy.py
   The tool is a configurable graph tool.
6. tests/units/front/test_shacl_facets_ui.py
   New. Structural contract for the popup partial, menu gating, loader
   count, detail-panel section, status icons/labels, and the canvas ring
   (drawn before seed / Find-Path highlights). Follows `.cursor/11` modal
   and status rules.
7. .planning/entity-shacl-facets/SPEC.md
   Shape count on `/api/v1/domain/classes`, client-side menu gating via
   `shaclShapeCountFor`, and the test plan updated to the written tests.

