## Implement entity SHACL facets (Explorer popup, panel, ring + MCP tool)
================================================================================

Context:
Implementation of `.planning/entity-shacl-facets/SPEC.md` against the
test-first contracts above. One entity is checked against every enabled SHACL
shape on its class, its ancestors and the whole graph, as entity-scoped SQL.
Surfaces: Graph Explorer right-click menu, detail-panel section, popup and
canvas ring; MCP tool `check_entity_shacl_facets`; REST `/nodes/shacl`.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/node/NodeShaclService.py
   New. Shape selection (own class, `parent` lineage, global), inherited
   shapes re-targeted to the entity's own class URI, one `UNION ALL` batch
   filtered on the entity with a per-shape fallback, five statuses, observed
   values (20-value cap), summary. An unreadable graph (never built) raises
   InfrastructureError with the engine message instead of a 500.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/node/NodeShaclResponse.py
   New. Pydantic response contract of `/nodes/shacl` (own file: the router is
   capped by the class-per-file ratchet).
