## Global code review: session secrets, session-debug masking, legacy session migrations
================================================================================

Context:
Global code review (`.cursorrules` review order). Guardrails green, session
data audited, README checked. The user approved the fixes below from the
first batch of findings. Finishing the registry Volume removal was stopped
before any edit: the volume is still part of `RegistryCfg.is_configured`,
the Lakebase `registries` row and the Initialize flow, so it needs a
decision of its own.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/domain/settings/WarehouseSettings.py
   `POST /settings/save` no longer stores a posted Databricks token in the
   session (`.cursor/07 §Domain Security`). No UI posted one; every reader
   already falls back to env / OAuth / OBO.
2. src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py
   Loading drops a `settings.databricks.token` left in an older session.
   Removed the pre-unified session migrations: `project_data` fallback key,
   `_migrate_legacy` (separate `ontology_config` / `mapping_config` /
   `design_layout` keys), `_migrate_top_level_renames` (`project` ->
   `domain`) and `_clear_legacy_keys`. File sessions expire after 24 h, so
   no such session can still exist; registry imports map fields themselves.
   Migrations that still apply to stored domains are kept.
3. src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py
   The DEBUG-only session dump masked `data["databricks"]["token"]`, a path
   that no longer exists, so a token under `settings.databricks` printed in
   clear. It now masks the real path without mutating the session.
4. src/back/objects/session/FileSessionMiddleware.py
   Debug logging reads only `domain_data` (dropped `project_data` fallback).
5. README.md
   Explorer paragraph mentions per-entity Data Quality Checks, SWRL business
   rules and Job class actions.
6. tests
   - tests/units/settings/test_v090_settings_warehouse.py: posted token ignored.
   - tests/units/domain/test_domain_session.py: token dropped on load;
     migration tests use the current session key.
