## Global code review, second batch: security, SQL escaping, dead code, plans
================================================================================

Context:
Second batch of review findings approved by the user (s1-s6, dead code,
medium findings, plans for structural items). Each fix landed with tests
written first; the integration pass tightened the size ratchet, refreshed the
docs and release notes, and ran the full suite.

Changes:

1. Permissions, reviews, cohort (S1)
   - src/back/objects/registry/PermissionService.py: permission updates read
     the row `FOR UPDATE`, so two concurrent edits cannot wipe each other.
   - src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/Catalog.py: a failed read
     raises instead of reading as "no permissions"; saves are transactional.
   - src/back/objects/registry/collab/ReviewService.py: quorum fails closed.
   - src/back/objects/digitaltwin/cohort/CohortService.py: the UC write probe
     quotes identifiers with `quote_uc_identifier`.
2. One dialect-aware SQL escape (S2)
   - src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py (+ __init__): `sql_escape(value,
     dialect)`, `sql_literal`, `is_sql_numeric`, `SQL_DIALECT_*`. Spark doubles
     backslashes then quotes; Postgres doubles quotes only.
   - SPARQLRuleEngine, DecisionTableEngine, AggregateRuleEngine, SHACLService,
     SparqlTranslator, GraphDBBackend, SWRLSQLTranslator use it; the store's
     `sql_flavor()` picks the dialect. `nan` / `inf` / `1_000` are quoted, a
     non-numeric aggregate `threshold` is rejected instead of pasted into
     HAVING. `_construct_to_sql` is back under the function budget.
   - src/back/core/w3c/shacl/ShapeConditions.py: rule conditions use
     `is_sql_numeric` on the SQL, in-memory and SPARQL paths.
3. Front-end XSS and dead JS (S3)
   - src/front/static/global/js/utils.js: one DOMPurify-sanitised
     `renderMarkdown`; quote-safe `escapeHtml` / `escapeAttr`. marked and
     DOMPurify pinned with SRI in base.html / ontology.html.
   - comments-panel, domain-collaboration, query-chat, ontology-assistant,
     domain-audit render through it; untrusted ontology / metadata values are
     escaped before `innerHTML`.
   - Six local quote-unsafe `escapeHtml` copies removed (registry-teams,
     home-tasks, settings-locks, settings-logs, settings-health,
     domain-review); 26 dead functions and uc-file-browser-modal.js deleted.
4. CSRF and /health (S4, S5)
   - src/shared/fastapi/csrf.py: unsafe methods need a non-empty cookie AND
     header, compared with `secrets.compare_digest` on bytes.
   - src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js: unload-time layout save
     uses `fetch(..., {keepalive: true})` (sendBeacon cannot carry the header).
   - src/shared/fastapi/health.py: `/health` runs local liveness checks only
     and returns no detail; readiness probes moved to the admin-only
     `GET /settings/diagnostics/readiness` (src/api/routers/internal/
     settings.py, settings-health.js, _settings_health.html). `_worst_status`
     helper; `_exc_text` reads `InfrastructureError.detail` so UC permission
     denials still get the GRANT hint.
   - run.py: the startup-failure fallback `/health` and `/` no longer return
     the traceback.
5. MCP (S6)
   - src/mcp-server/server/http_client.py, tools.py: GraphQL paths
     URL-encode the domain name and forward the caller's identity; HTTP errors
     become a short message (`http_errors_as_text`).
   - src/mcp-server/server/resources.py: `_fetch_json` gives every resource
     the same short error JSON.
6. Dead Python code and false-success errors
   - 63 verified-unused symbols deleted across DatabricksClient,
     DocumentExtractor, AgentClient, GraphDBBackend, DeltaBase,
     _table_naming, SyncedTableManager, Mapping, registry store base +
     Lakebase store, DomainSession, GlobalConfigService, TaskContext,
     internal/dtwin.py, digitaltwin/__init__.py (14 wrappers), DigitalTwin
     (20 forwarders), back/core/__init__.py, task_manager.
   - Old `project` key fallbacks removed in internal/ontology.py, domains.py,
     HomeService.py.
   - SHACLService: an unparseable report raises InfrastructureError instead of
     "conforms". UnityCatalog / MetadataService: failed listings raise instead
     of returning an empty schema; callers re-raise (502) or log per table.
7. Plans
   - .planning/code-review-2026-10-14/PLAN.md (new): ten structural items
     with evidence, target design, migration, tests, priority (P0-P2),
     including the registry Volume removal and the scheduled-build
     `last_build` rewrite.
8. Docs and release notes
   - docs/deployment.md, docs/development.md: `/health` vs readiness.
   - docs/architecture.md, docs/api.md: CSRF rejection rules.
   - docs/backend.md, docs/diagrams/class-hierarchy.mmd: deleted methods.
   - releases/ReleaseNotes_V0.9.0.md: "Security hardening (code review)"
     section, behaviour-change upgrade notes (health probes, CSRF,
     `sh:pattern` backslashes, UC errors), test status.
9. Tests
